s-single responsibilty principle
Class should have only one responsiablity.
One class can have more than on method but should handle same responsiablity.
for example: database class, should only perform operation related to database.

O- open close principle(OCP)
A class should be open for extension but close for modification.
never touch old method, you can add new method in new class.
Example:
we can achive this by making class as interface and abstract, after that just override the method.

interface PaymentMethod {
    void pay();
}

class CreditCardPayment implements PaymentMethod {
    @Override
    public void play() { System.out.println("Processing credit card..."); }
}

class CashPayment implements PaymentMethod {
    @Override
    public void pay() { System.out.println("Processing cash..."); }
}


L- Liskov substiution principle(LSP)
subclasses should be subsitutable for their base classes.
we can able to access all the feature of superclass by calling subclass.
Guidline to follow LSP
1.Signature rule
-Method Argument Rule
Parent class and child class must have method with same signature, if want to override parent class method.

- return type Rule
you can add return type either child type or it's supper class, but not supper to supper class return type.
class Book { 
    public String getContent() { return "Standard Book Text"; }
}
class EBook extends Book { 
    public String getDownloadUrl() { return "https://example.com"; }
}

class Library {
    public Book borrowItem() {
        return new Book();
    }
}

// Subclass adhering to LSP (Covariant return type)
class DigitalLibrary extends Library {
    @Override
    public EBook borrowItem() { // Valid: EBook is a subtype of Book
        return new EBook();
    }
}

-exception type rules
subclass should throw either same type or it's child class type exception.

2.property rule
